{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"4142","artifact_type":"feature-context","name":"plan/feature-context-itsaplan-work-item-backend.md@sha256:033e38472a6eef4360cee6c2bdfc10fe844df2ab829ff76542eaa96f284c482b"},"owner_reference":"4142","content":"# ARTIFACT:DISCOVERY\n\n## Feature\n\nItsaplan work-item backend availability.\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nA Development Harness user who operates an Itsaplan instance cannot select it as the configured backlog provider, so work-item lifecycle operations remain tied to another provider despite Itsaplan exposing REST and MCP interfaces for issue work.\n\n## Goals\n\n1. A configured Itsaplan-backed environment can use the supported DH work-item lifecycle without consumers selecting a separate store for work items, plans, or artifacts.\n2. Provider-native limitations, identities, pagination, authentication, availability, and milestone behavior are surfaced accurately rather than inferred from GitHub semantics.\n\n## Anti-Goals\n\n1. Provisioning an Itsaplan instance, granting permissions, or running Itsaplan agents/runners.\n2. Selecting REST or MCP transport, mapping cycles or initiatives to milestones, or defining implementation architecture.\n3. Making #4143 a prerequisite: runner integration is a distinct concern.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional\n\n1. Work-item records support the lifecycle information DH exposes: title, description, status, labels, comments, grooming sections, dependencies, and provider references.\n2. Plan and artifact records preserve the unified routed-backend ownership required by DH, or unsupported capability is explicit.\n3. Bounded discovery/listing and stable opaque identities retain correct paging and ownership semantics.\n4. Authentication and authorization failure states are distinguishable from missing records.\n\n### Non-Functional\n\n1. Provider behavior is validated against the current upstream OpenAPI/API implementation and does not rely on undocumented endpoint shapes.\n2. Provider availability and pending-write behavior follow the DH remote-provider contract or report the capability gap.\n3. No automated runner is configured or invoked by this scope.\n\n## Design Questions for Planning\n\n1. Evaluate REST versus MCP transport only after capability and stability evidence is compared.\n2. Evaluate whether Itsaplan has a native milestone equivalent compatible with DHs numeric milestone contract; do not assume cycles or initiatives are equivalent.\n3. Evaluate how DH logical plan and artifact content maps to Itsaplan-owned records, documents, or another documented provider capability without creating a second consumer-selected backend.\n\n## References\n\n- research/task-management/itsaplan.md (2026-10-17)\n- https://github.com/croffasia/itsaplan\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_types.py\n- plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md\n- #1177 and #3262\n\n## Resolved Questions\n\n| Question | Answer | Source |\n|----------|--------|--------|\n| Is Itsaplan an issue-tracking provider with external APIs? | Yes; upstream README advertises REST/OpenAPI and MCP, and source exposes POST /mcp. | upstream README and apps/api/src/mcp/mount.ts |\n| Does this grooming authorize its runner? | No. | assignment scope |\n| Are #4142 and #4143 a hard dependency pair? | No; they cover backend provider and runner concerns respectively. | assignment scope |\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- Which currently supported Itsaplan release/API schema and target instance URL will be used by a future implementation?\n- Does the selected instance/API expose a native milestone-compatible entity and, if not, what human-approved behavior is required?\n- Can Itsaplan provide DH logical plan and artifact content with revision/conflict semantics, or must that capability be reported unsupported?\n\n## User Confirmation\n\n- [x] Requested grooming defines this discovery scope; unresolved choices are recorded for later planning."}